
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">John Heil, emeritus professor of philosophy at Washington University in St. Louis and Durham University, has died.</p>



<span id="more-27491"></span>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img decoding="async" width="1024" height="881" src="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Heil-John-photo-1024x881.png" alt="" class="wp-image-27492" style="aspect-ratio:1.162321986224004;width:549px;height:auto" srcset="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Heil-John-photo-1024x881.png 1024w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Heil-John-photo-300x258.png 300w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Heil-John-photo-768x661.png 768w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Heil-John-photo-1536x1321.png 1536w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Heil-John-photo-250x215.png 250w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Heil-John-photo.png 1888w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://philosophy.washu.edu/people/john-heilFAHA" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Professor Heil</a> was well-known for his work in metaphysics and philosophy of mind. He is the author of <em>From an Ontological Point of View</em> (Oxford University Press 2006), <em>The Universe as We Find It</em> (Oxford University Press 2012), <em>Appearance in Reality</em> (Oxford University Press 2021), <em>What is Metaphysics?</em> (Polity Press 2021), and <em>Relations</em> (Cambridge University Press 2021), among many other works. You can learn more about his writings <a href="https://philpeople.org/profiles/john-heil" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">here</a>. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Prior to joining the faculty at Washington University in St. Louis, Heil was a longtime member of the Department of Philosophy at Davidson College, and before that, Virginia Commonwealth University. He has held honorary and visiting appointments at many universities, including Monash University, the University of Oxford, the University of Otago, the University of Cape Town, University of the Witwatersrand, and the University of Rochester. He earned his PhD at Vanderbilt University, and his BA from Randolph Macon College.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">You can read an interview with Professor Heil about his work at <em><a href="https://www.3-16am.co.uk/articles/the-universe-as-we-find-it" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">3:16am</a></em>. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">John Heil died on October 27, 2026.</p>



